"""KS3 selections from the existing Prodigy GCSE science practicals."""
LABS=[]
def lab(id,title,subject,keys,change,measure,control,extension=False):
 LABS.append(dict(id=id,title=title,subject=subject,keys=keys.split(),goals=[change,measure,control],extension=extension))
lab('bmic','Microscopy','Biology','microscope cell specialised','Start with low magnification and bring the image into focus.','Observe the cell boundary, cytoplasm and nucleus; compare samples.','Change one control at a time. Use the scale before estimating cell size.')
lab('bosm','Osmosis in potato tissue','Biology','diffusion','Compare the effect of solution concentration on potato mass.','Record starting and final masses; look for a gain or loss.','Keep tissue dimensions, time, temperature and solution volume consistent.')
lab('bfood','Food tests','Biology','food-tests nutrition','Choose a food sample and a test. Predict the result first.','Observe the colour change or precipitate; record the evidence.','Use separate samples and appropriate positive/negative controls.')
lab('benz','Enzymes and pH','Biology','digestion catalyst','Change pH and test how quickly amylase breaks down starch.','Use iodine evidence to identify when starch is no longer detected.','Keep enzyme amount, starch amount and temperature consistent.')
lab('bphot','Pondweed photosynthesis','Biology','photosynthesis leaf plant-practical variables','Change lamp distance and collect repeated oxygen readings.','Compare gas output over the same time interval.','Keep temperature and carbon dioxide availability consistent.')
lab('breac','Reaction-time investigation','Biology','planning data drugs','Compare ruler-drop reaction times under controlled conditions.','Record repeats and compare a representative average.','Keep release method and starting hand position consistent. Avoid anticipation.')
lab('bfield','Quadrats and field sampling','Biology','ecosystem foodweb biodiversity','Use quadrats to sample plant abundance across a habitat.','Compare counts and calculate an estimate using the area sampled.','Choose positions fairly; keep frame size and counting rules consistent.')
lab('salt','Making salt crystals','Chemistry','neutral filter reaction','Follow reaction, filtration, concentration and crystallisation stages.','Observe which material remains on the filter and where crystals form.','A real heating experiment requires the teacher’s method and risk assessment.')
lab('elec','Electrolysis: extraction extension','Chemistry','extraction charge','Compare how an electric current can change suitable compounds.','Observe the products at each electrode; record the differences.','Year 9 extension: focus on observations before exploring the GCSE ion explanations.',True)
lab('temp','Temperature changes in reactions','Chemistry','chemical-energy acid neutral','Change the reacting amount and watch the temperature.','Compare starting and final temperatures, using the same timing rule.','Keep starting conditions and insulation consistent; repeat the comparison.')
lab('rate','Reaction-rate investigation','Chemistry','acid catalyst combustion variables','Change concentration and compare the rate of gas production.','Record gas volume against time and compare the initial change.','Keep reactant amount, temperature and apparatus consistent.')
lab('chrom','Paper chromatography','Chemistry','distil atoms','Place a small spot on a pencil line above the solvent.','Observe how the ink components separate as the solvent rises.','Keep solvent conditions consistent; mark its final position promptly.')
lab('water','Water purification and distillation','Chemistry','distil filter solution','Compare filtration, evaporation and distillation.','Track where insoluble solids, dissolved substances and solvent go.','Use the method suited to the mixture; a clear liquid is not proof of purity.')
lab('shc','Heating different materials','Physics','thermal energy food-energy','Compare temperature rises for a controlled energy input.','Observe how mass and material affect heating.','The specific-heat-capacity calculation is optional Year 9 extension work.',True)
lab('rs','Resistance in a wire','Physics','voltage current','Change wire length while keeping other conditions consistent.','Measure current and potential difference; compare resistance.','Keep material and cross-section the same and avoid heating the wire.')
lab('iv','Current and potential difference','Physics','voltage current','Change potential difference and compare different components.','Take paired current and voltage readings and look for a pattern.','Control temperature where possible; not every component has constant resistance.')
lab('de','Measuring density','Physics','particles planning pressure','Measure mass and find the volume of a regular or irregular object.','Compare mass divided by volume, with consistent units.','Check the balance zero and read liquid scales at eye level.')
lab('sp','Force and spring extension','Physics','spring force investigate-bungee','Add a load, allow it to settle and measure the spring length.','Subtract the original length to find extension; take repeats.','Keep the same spring and stay within a safe, proportional range.')
lab('ac','Trolley motion: extension investigation','Physics','speed dt force gravity','Compare trolley motion when a force or mass is changed.','Use the timing readings to describe changes in motion.','Year 9 extension: formal acceleration calculations go beyond the core speed task.',True)
lab('wv','Wave speed, frequency and wavelength','Physics','waves sound','Change frequency and observe the wave pattern.','Measure wavelength and compare frequency × wavelength.','Distinguish the moving wave from the local oscillation of the medium.')
lab('lt','Reflection and refraction','Physics','light colour','Change a light ray’s angle at a mirror or transparent block.','Measure angles from the normal and compare directions.','Keep the block and reference normal fixed while comparing rays.')
lab('ir','Infrared radiation','Physics','convection thermal em','Compare surfaces under the same temperature conditions.','Observe differences in emitted or detected infrared radiation.','Keep distance, orientation and temperature consistent for a fair comparison.')
lab('insulation','Thermal insulation','Physics','convection thermal investigate-conduction','Compare insulating materials around a container of warm water.','Record cooling over equal time intervals.','Keep water mass, starting temperature, exposed area and lid conditions consistent.')
